## Prompt
Task 01 — Web server down
The httpd service should be running now and start automatically on boot.
Right now it does neither. Fix it.

## Break

# System will install httpd if not installed. Then stop any running instances and disable running in background 
sudo dnf install -y httpd
sudo systemctl stop httpd && sudo systemctl disable httpd

## Variable 
enabled=$(sudo systemctl is-enabled httpd)
active=$(sudo systemctl is-active httpd)

## Check
 
$enabled = sudo systemctl is-enabled httpd
$active = sudo systemctl is-active httpd

# If user successfully allows httpd to run in background then reward them 1 point otherwise reward them 0 points 
if sudo systemctl is-enabled httpd 
then echo "Task 1.1: Pass -- httpd is enabled (+1)" | tee -a check.txt
else echo "Task 1.1: Fail -- http not enabled (-1)" | tee -a check.txt 
fi

# If user successfully starts httpd then reward them 1 point otherwise reward them 0 points 
if sudo systemctl is-active httpd
then echo "Task 1.2:Pass -- httpd is active (+1)" | tee -a check.txt 
else echo "Task 1.2: Fail -- httpd not active" | tee -a check.txt 
fi
